#! ia 1.0

@kind governance
  meaning
    says "A standing 'ought' — a norm that always holds (law · principle · convention · policy-as-norm)."
    answers "Is this record a binding rule, rather than a thing or an action?"
  data
    order 0
    lane authority

@kind contract
  meaning
    says "An obligation that another record relies on: a structural body schema or a signature between parties. The schema and contract discriminators have distinct dialects under this shared kind."
    answers "Does this record pin a structure that something else relies on?"
  data
    order 1
    lane contracts
    authority-lane authority

@kind definition
  meaning
    says "The meaning of a term or the membership of an axis (kind · lane · category · predicate · primitive · topology nodes)."
    answers "Does this record define what a word or an axis-value means?"
  data
    order 2
    lane definitions

@kind template
  meaning
    says "A reusable output shape. An implemented consumer is required to instantiate it into records or files."
    answers "Does this record generate other records?"
  data
    order 3
    lane templates

@kind check
  meaning
    says "A declared evaluation gate. Its bound evaluator produces a verdict; the declaration alone does not execute."
    answers "Does this record execute and yield a verdict?"
  data
    order 4
    lane enforcement

@kind policy
  meaning
    says "An access or routing rule — who may, and what flows where."
    answers "Does this record decide permission or routing?"
  data
    order 5
    lane enforcement

@kind binding
  meaning
    says "An explicit connection between an actor, invocation or trigger and behavior. A host consumer supplies execution."
    answers "Does this record wire something executable to when it fires?"
  data
    order 6
    lane bindings

